  "question": {
    "text": "Suppose that $f(0)=-3$ and $f^{\\prime}(x) \\leq 5$ for all values of $x$ Then, the largest value which $f(2)$ can attain is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "7",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "10",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "2",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "9",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Using LMVT in [0,2] $\\frac{f(2)-f(0)}{2-0}=f^{\\prime}(c),$ where $c \\in(0,2)$\r\n\r\n$\\frac{f(2)+3}{2} \\leq 5 \\Rightarrow f(2) \\leq 7$"
  }
}